{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Also you shall give into our hand.</b> It is difficult: how could the servant of HaShem ask for sacrifices to Elohim from a despised and defiled man who exalted his mouth against the Holy One of Israel — in addition to his being a foreigner? Does HaShem desire the sacrifice of the wicked? And even though the Torah said ״אִישׁ אִישׁ״ to include them (Ḥullin 13b), yet only not to request from him." "Indeed, the words of a wise man — he was precise in his language and said <b>and we shall do</b>, when he should have said ״to do for HaShem our Elohim.״ Rather, he intended to say that he should give into their hand livestock fit for sacrifices, and we shall do for HaShem our Elohim for our own needs — except that he would provide them a gift from which they would supply their sacrifices to HaShem. Also by this it is not difficult that he said ״sacrifices and burnt offerings״ for the Tanna who said (Menachot 73a) that they do not accept from the nations of the world except burnt offerings and not peace offerings — and here the verse is full, as it says ״sacrifices and burnt offerings״ — but according to our words it is not difficult."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:28.248938624Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}